From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:26:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: exp - Dynamic Activation of Brain candidate
 (behavior-start throttle)

Clean-room extension of the already-shipped PetalReduceSensorWorkConfig
technique (entity-id-phased skip), applied to Brain's dominant cost instead
of Sensor: only Brain#startEachNonRunningBehavior ("should this entity start
something new") is throttled, phased per entity so the population does not
pause in lockstep. tickEachRunningBehavior always runs every tick - an
already-running behavior's internal state is never skipped mid-flight.

This is the D-57 alternative candidate to worker-pool parallelization
(DECISIONS.md D-57): load shedding instead of cross-thread dispatch, so it
does not hit the per-task dispatch overhead this session measured as larger
than a single Sensor tick's real cost.

Default off (-Dlophinya.loadshed.brainBehaviorStartThrottle=false).

exp/* isolated exploration branch per DEC-69. Not for merge into ver/26.2-nya.

diff --git a/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/loadshed/BrainBehaviorStartThrottleConfig.java b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/loadshed/BrainBehaviorStartThrottleConfig.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4860dc3bc26da8c888ac021ea9f0ef0174214db0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/loadshed/BrainBehaviorStartThrottleConfig.java
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+package fun.bm.lophinya.loadshed;
+
+/**
+ * Lophinya: throttle how often {@code Brain#tick} checks whether to start a new behavior
+ * (DEC-69, "Dynamic Activation of Brain" candidate).
+ *
+ * <p>Clean-room extension of the same technique {@code PetalReduceSensorWorkConfig} already
+ * ships in this fork (entity-id-phased skip, so different entities skip on different ticks
+ * instead of the whole population pausing together) - applied here to the dominant AI cost this
+ * project's own profiling found (Brain Behavior Tick, ~60-70% of a Brain-having entity's tick
+ * budget - see project-docs/evidence/20260805-region-parallel-tick-topology.md 6.1), instead of
+ * to Sensor.
+ *
+ * <p>Deliberately narrower than "skip Brain tick entirely": only the START check
+ * ({@code Brain#startEachNonRunningBehavior} - "should this entity begin a new behavior right
+ * now") is throttled. An already-running behavior is ticked every tick without exception, so its
+ * internal state (duration timers, {@code canStillUse} checks) is never skipped mid-flight - the
+ * only user-visible effect is a delayed reaction to *starting* something new, on entities that
+ * have nothing running yet.
+ *
+ * <pre>
+ *   -Dlophinya.loadshed.brainBehaviorStartThrottle=true   # enabled. DEFAULT OFF
+ *   -Dlophinya.loadshed.brainBehaviorStartThrottleTicks=10 # check every Nth tick per entity
+ * </pre>
+ */
+public final class BrainBehaviorStartThrottleConfig {
+
+    public static final boolean ENABLED =
+        "true".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("lophinya.loadshed.brainBehaviorStartThrottle", "false"));
+
+    public static final int DELAY_TICKS =
+        Integer.getInteger("lophinya.loadshed.brainBehaviorStartThrottleTicks", 10);
+
+    private BrainBehaviorStartThrottleConfig() {
+    }
+}
